{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2821"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of agricultural and forestry machinery"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2821"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agricultural-forestry-machinery/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :mechanical-safety :hydraulic-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :agricultural-forestry-machinery-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :eda :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "AgMachAdvisor ⊣ Agricultural and Forestry Machinery Plant Operations
 Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant
 OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for agricultural/forestry-machinery
 manufacturing (tractor-component/harvester/tillage-equipment assembly
 and test lines producing finished tractors, combine harvesters,
 tillage implements, balers and forestry harvesters) -- not direct
 assembly/test-bench-equipment control authority and not
 machinery-safety-certification authority (e.g. CE marking under the
 EU Machinery Directive, or ROPS certification under the OECD Standard
 Codes for the Official Testing of Agricultural and Forestry
 Tractors). Four ops (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance`
 / `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct assembly/
 test-bench-equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block,
 permanent safety-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues a machinery safety certification mark), independent
 equipment verification/registration before maintenance scheduling,
 independent batch verification/registration before shipment
 coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute against the
 batch's own logged production quantity, double-schedule guard,
 product-type validation, PTO no-load-speed plausibility validation,
 and defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 (mechanical-safety/hydraulic-hazard/PTO-guard-compliance concern)
 ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch`
 is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
